{
  "name": "Plan fee with included usage, overage billed above the allowance",
  "description": "A $500/month Growth plan includes 100,000 API calls. Billing the plan fee also grants the month's included calls as a lot on a capacity ledger (the template's `included` allowance), expiring at the end of the month. The usage activity draws accepted calls from that lot first and bills only the excess at $2.00 per 1,000: 150,000 September calls consume all 100,000 included calls and bill $100 of overage (4120 usage revenue), earned when the measurement is accepted. The fee is earned over the month as subscription revenue (4110). September revenue is $600, MRR stays $500 (overage is not recurring), and the capacity report shows 100,000 consumed, none free. Record the measurement before the lot expires: one recorded after expiry finds no included calls and bills every call as overage. An allowance lot's expiry is a term on its grant, so each month's allowance is its own grant: this contract covers the September period.",
